        -512,
        336
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Parallel Sheet Parsing\n\nEach sheet has a different structure:\n- **Sheet 1:** Headers at row 16, analyst in col 0 & col 23\n- **Sheet 2:** Headers at row 2, analyst in col 0\n- **Sheet 3:** Headers at row 2, may be empty\n- **Sheet 4:** Headers at row 2, analyst in col 0\n\nSheet 5 is informational only — not parsed here.\n\n⚠️ The `range` parameter tells each node where data starts.\n⚠️ Sheet names must match EXACTLY (they include parentheses).",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 320
      },
      "id": "sticky_parse",
      "name": "Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -96,
        -144
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Normalization Logic\n\nThe Code node handles:\n1. Column name differences across sheets\n2. Parsing analyst format: `TMONTAGUE;jjeffrey`\n3. Skipping header/subtotal rows (CASE_1, etc)\n4. Building a uniform tracker record with:\n   - Security identification\n   - Analyst assignment (primary + supporting)\n   - Key financial data for context\n   - Tracking fields (status, confirmedBy, etc)\n\n**Next step:** Connect output to your tracker store (SharePoint list, Excel file, or database).",
